  "analysis": "The previous approach assumes a purely quadratic growth for large k, which fails in edge cases where the obstacle set traps the knight in a finite component (e.g., blocking all 8 first-move squares around the origin). In such cases, the number of reachable squares remains constant after the diameter of the component. To robustly handle all cases (infinite vs finite components), I propose a bounded BFS that:\n- Uses a fixed bounding box large enough to detect escape to infinity if possible (BOUND = 30 is safe since obstacles are within [-10,10]).\n- Detects whether the origin can reach outside the obstacle region (|x|>10 or |y|>10).\n- If escape is possible (infinite component), use the same extrapolation as before: ans(k) = 4k^2 + 4k + C for large k, with C derived from BFS up to LIM (e.g., 100).\n- If escape is not possible (finite component), compute the exact component size and diameter from BFS within the bounded box, and answer exactly for any k: if k <= diameter, count nodes with dist <= k; otherwise return the full component size.\nThis approach guarantees correctness for all valid inputs, including traps and large k with obstacles.",
  "plan": "Implement a robust BFS-based solver:\n- Set BOUND = 30 to cover the obstacle region and potential escape paths; grid size will be (2*BOUND+1)^2 ≈ 61x61.\n- Mark blocked cells within the bound from the input; origin is guaranteed not blocked.\n- Perform a BFS from (0,0) using a 2D dist array (offset by BOUND).\n- Track: (a) infinite flag if any visited cell has |x|>10 or |y|>10, (b) counts by distance up to LIM (e.g., LIM = 100), (c) max distance seen (diameter) and total component size when finite.\n- If infinite:\n  - Build prefix ans_k for k in [0..LIM] from counts.\n  - Compute C = ans_k[LIM] - (4*LIM^2 + 4*LIM) mod M.\n  - If k <= LIM, output ans_k[k]; else output (4*k^2 + 4*k + C) mod M.\n- If finite:\n  - If k <= diameter, count grid cells with dist <= k; else output total component size (mod M).\n- Also keep a fast-path: if n == 0, answer is 1 + 4*k*(k+1) mod M.\n- Compile and test with provided samples and edge cases.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > main.cpp <<'CPP'\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nstatic const long long MOD = 1000000007LL;\n\nint main(){\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long k; int n;\n    if(!(cin >> k >> n)) return 0;\n    vector<pair<int,int>> obstacles(n);\n    for(int i=0;i<n;i++){ int x,y; cin >> x >> y; obstacles[i] = {x,y}; }\n\n    // Fast-path: no obstacles\n    if(n == 0){\n        long long km = k % MOD;\n        long long ans = ( (4LL * km) % MOD * ((km + 1) % MOD) ) % MOD; // 4*k*(k+1)\n        ans = (ans + 1) % MOD; // +1\n        cout << ans << '\\n';\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    const int BOUND = 30;                    // bounding box [-BOUND, BOUND]\n    const int SIZE = 2*BOUND + 1;            // grid size per dimension\n    const int LIM = 100;                       // precompute up to LIM moves exactly\n\n    // 2D grids for blocked and distance\n    vector<vector<char>> blocked(SIZE, vector<char>(SIZE, 0));\n    auto inb = [&](int x, int y){ return -BOUND <= x && x <= BOUND && -BOUND <= y && y <= BOUND; };\n    for(auto &p : obstacles){\n        int x = p.first, y = p.second;\n        if(inb(x,y)) blocked[x+BOUND][y+BOUND] = 1;\n    }\n    // origin is guaranteed not blocked by problem statement\n    blocked[0+BOUND][0+BOUND] = 0;\n\n    vector<vector<int>> dist(SIZE, vector<int>(SIZE, -1));\n    queue<pair<int,int>> q;\n    dist[0+BOUND][0+BOUND] = 0;\n    q.push({0,0});\n\n    const int dx[8] = {1,1,2,2,-1,-1,-2,-2};\n    const int dy[8] = {2,-2,1,-1,2,-2,1,-1};\n\n    vector<long long> counts(LIM+1, 0); // number of cells exactly at distance d\n    bool infinite = false;\n    int maxd = 0;\n\n    while(!q.empty()){\n        auto cur = q.front(); q.pop();\n        int x = cur.first, y = cur.second;\n        int d = dist[x+BOUND][y+BOUND];\n        if(d <= LIM) counts[d]++;\n        if(abs(x) > 10 || abs(y) > 10) infinite = true; // escaped obstacle region\n        if(d == LIM) continue;\n        for(int i=0;i<8;i++){\n            int nx = x + dx[i], ny = y + dy[i];\n            if(!inb(nx, ny)) continue;\n            if(blocked[nx+BOUND][ny+BOUND]) continue;\n            if(dist[nx+BOUND][ny+BOUND] != -1) continue;\n            dist[nx+BOUND][ny+BOUND] = d+1;\n            maxd = max(maxd, d+1);\n            q.push({nx, ny});\n        }\n    }\n\n    // If infinite, we can extrapolate using the quadratic form with constant C\n    if(infinite){\n        // Prefix sums: number of cells with distance <= t for t in [0..LIM]\n        vector<long long> ans_k(LIM+1, 0);\n        long long cum = 0;\n        for(int i=0;i<=LIM;i++){ cum += counts[i]; ans_k[i] = cum; }\n\n        long long L = LIM;\n        long long quad = 4*(L*L) + 4*L; // 4L^2 + 4L\n        long long C = (ans_k[LIM] - quad) % MOD;\n        if(C < 0) C += MOD;\n\n        long long result;\n        if(k <= LIM){\n            result = ans_k[(int)k] % MOD;\n        } else {\n            long long kmod = k % MOD;\n            __int128 t = ( (__int128)kmod * kmod ) % MOD;\n            long long term = (4LL * (long long)t) % MOD; // 4*k^2\n            term = (term + 4LL * kmod) % MOD;        // + 4k\n            term = (term + C) % MOD;                  // + C\n            result = term;\n        }\n        cout << (result % MOD + MOD) % MOD << \"\\n\";\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    // Finite component: determine exact size and diameter from dist grid\n    long long total = 0;\n    int max_distance_seen = 0;\n    for(int i=0;i<SIZE;i++){\n        for(int j=0;j<SIZE;j++){\n            if(dist[i][j] != -1){ total++; max_distance_seen = max(max_distance_seen, dist[i][j]); }\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long answer;\n    if(k <= max_distance_seen){\n        long long cnt = 0;\n        for(int i=0;i<SIZE;i++){\n            for(int j=0;j<SIZE;j++){\n                if(dist[i][j] != -1 && dist[i][j] <= k) cnt++;\n            }\n        }\n        answer = cnt % MOD;\n    } else {\n        answer = total % MOD;\n    }\n\n    cout << (answer % MOD + MOD) % MOD << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\nCPP\n",
